1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,420
THIS PROGRAM CONTAINS AI-GENERATED CONTENT

2
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:06,048
[♪ dramatic music playing]

3
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:08,258
[screams]

4
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:20,686
CASE 2:
GWANDONG BYEOLGOK: THE EXILE MURDER CASE

5
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,731
[♪ theme song playing]

6
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:29,904
MURDER CLUB: LIAR'S TABLE

7
00:00:29,905 --> 00:00:30,988
[person 1 exclaims]

8
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:32,615
FIRST PLAYER ENTERS

9
00:00:32,616 --> 00:00:33,741
What's all this?

10
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:35,159
EOM JIYOON
COMEDIAN

11
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,620
So this is what it looks like.

12
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:38,704
FASCINATING

13
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:39,706
[exclaims]

14
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:42,500
We're playing a board game like this?

15
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:44,210
When it comes to board games, I'm really…

16
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:45,419
[person 2] Hello.

17
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,255
It's our second time meeting, right?

18
00:00:47,256 --> 00:00:48,464
- We met once before.
- Yes.

19
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:50,341
- How have you been?
- The same old.

20
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:51,425
PANI BOTTLE
YOUTUBER

21
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:53,970
You're a pro at survival games.

22
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:55,264
- Me?
- Yes.

23
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,431
Are you mistaking me for someone else?

24
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:59,977
I'm the worst at survival games.

25
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:03,479
I'm known for being totally useless.

26
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,107
- I thought I was early, but I'm third.
- [Pani Bottle] Hello.

27
00:01:06,108 --> 00:01:07,191
- [Jiyoon] Hello.
- Hey there.

28
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:08,943
- I enjoy your work.
- [Jiyoon] Thank you.

29
00:01:08,944 --> 00:01:10,319
You've done this before, right?

30
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:11,654
We both did it together.

31
00:01:11,655 --> 00:01:13,281
It was so funny. I laughed so much.

32
00:01:13,282 --> 00:01:15,825
He slapped the culprit
in the back of the head at one point.

33
00:01:15,826 --> 00:01:17,201
- [Yangrak] Be careful.
- For being guilty?

34
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:19,538
You were there at 2:17 a.m.,
looking right at the camera.

35
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:22,081
- Wait a minute.
- I've got chills.

36
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,709
- You little!
- [others chuckling]

37
00:01:24,293 --> 00:01:25,793
Why did you hit me?

38
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:27,420
[Kim Doyun] He got physical!

39
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:28,504
Why did you hit me?

40
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:29,672
- I was sure it was him.
- [Pani Bottle chuckles]

41
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:30,756
HIS HUNCH WAS ACCURATE

42
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:32,092
We all cracked up.

43
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,135
- Hello.
- [Jiyoon] Hello.

44
00:01:34,136 --> 00:01:35,386
- All in a good mood.
- Hello.

45
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:36,637
- Hello.
- [Yangrak] My gosh.

46
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:38,974
- You're as tall as a basketball player.
- Nice to see you.

47
00:01:39,558 --> 00:01:42,768
[Jiyoon]
He's got an unfair advantage as an actor.

48
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:44,729
I'm the only one who's never acted here.

49
00:01:44,730 --> 00:01:47,774
[inhales deeply]
This is bad. I'm a terrible actor.

50
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:49,483
Aren't you acting now?

51
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:51,444
- You're acting as we speak.
- [chuckles] Playing pretend.

52
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:52,528
- You're acting now.
- Me?

53
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:54,239
I'm really not.

54
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:56,700
- [person 5] Hello.
- [Jiyoon] Hello. Oh, my gosh!

55
00:01:57,492 --> 00:01:59,744
- [Pani Bottle] You're a chef, right?
- [Jiyoon] Mr. Iron Arms.

56
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:01,662
Yes, I was on <i>Culinary Class Wars</i>.

57
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,372
My nickname was Iron Arms.

58
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:04,707
Forget everything else,

59
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:06,208
when this is over, can we get a table?

60
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:07,585
- Yes, can we get an invite?
- [Yangrak chuckles]

61
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:08,836
- Of course.
- [Jiyoon] Seriously.

62
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:10,254
Can we go today after filming?

63
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,339
- Sure.
- [others chuckle]

64
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,673
TALKED INTO A TEAM DINNER

65
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:14,300
- [radio static]
- What's happening?

66
00:02:14,301 --> 00:02:15,635
STARTLED

67
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:19,138
[host]
<i>Welcome to</i> Murder Club: Liar's Table<i>.</i>

68
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:21,307
<i>This is a special space</i>

69
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:24,143
<i>where you'll play a game
called "Murder Mystery."</i>

70
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:27,897
<i>In today's Murder Mystery,</i>

71
00:02:27,898 --> 00:02:32,610
<i>you will try to identify
the culprit hidden among you.</i>

72
00:02:32,611 --> 00:02:35,529
<i>You will each be assigned a unique role</i>

73
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,782
<i>and play the game as that character.</i>

74
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:39,700
<i>There is only one culprit,</i>

75
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:43,245
<i>but every player has their own secret.</i>

76
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,997
<i>To win this game,</i>

77
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:49,293
<i>you are allowed to lie, conceal the truth,
and act deceptively.</i>

78
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:52,254
<i>The game consists of five rounds.</i>

79
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:53,964
<i>At the start of each round,</i>

80
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:56,467
<i>one clue will be revealed
to the entire group,</i>

81
00:02:56,468 --> 00:02:58,803
<i>and all the players will pick out</i>

82
00:02:58,804 --> 00:03:01,347
<i>one card clue and one object clue.</i>

83
00:03:01,348 --> 00:03:03,474
<i>The card clues are confidential</i>

84
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:08,145
<i>and can only be shared
during private conversations.</i>

85
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:11,899
<i>The object clues
can be examined by all players.</i>

86
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:16,487
<i>After collecting the clues,
you will have a 15-minute discussion.</i>

87
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:19,699
<i>Starting Round 2, you will have time
for private conversations.</i>

88
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,827
<i>After the group discussion,
you will have five minutes</i>

89
00:03:22,828 --> 00:03:24,745
<i>to talk secretly
in the private conversation zones.</i>

90
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:27,957
<i>In Round 5, the final round,
you will make your final vote.</i>

91
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:29,542
<i>After the final group discussion,</i>

92
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:33,171
<i>you will vote for the person
you suspect to be the culprit.</i>

93
00:03:33,964 --> 00:03:36,133
<i>Now, you will be assigned your roles.</i>

94
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:39,511
<i>Please choose one of the files
in front of you.</i>

95
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,931
This seems to be
the only female character.

96
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,015
- Yun Suyeon?
- Yes.

97
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:47,393
- I'll pick my favorite color, orange.
- [Yangrak] Gosh.

98
00:03:47,394 --> 00:03:48,644
[Juseong] I feel like I should be Musoe.

99
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:49,728
[Jiyoon] Since it means "iron."

100
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:52,398
A character named Bokgil?
Since it's set in the Joseon era…

101
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:53,524
Isn't Bokgil a dog's name?

102
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:55,193
- [Jiyoon] Maybe it's a Jindo.
- "Come here, Bokgil!"

103
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:58,905
THE CULPRIT HAS BEEN CHOSEN

104
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:00,574
I'm Yun Igyeong.

105
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:03,033
[Yangrak] Is Yun Igyeong

106
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:04,785
- some kind of nobleman?
- I am, yes.

107
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:06,620
- "An exiled official."
- A public official.

108
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:08,497
I'm high-ranking, but I've been exiled.

109
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:10,500
[♪ dramatic music playing]

110
00:04:13,003 --> 00:04:14,086
YUN IGYEONG

111
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:15,588
AGE 40, FORMER LOCAL OFFICIAL,
IN EXILE

112
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:18,132
And Yun Suyeon is my daughter.

113
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:19,384
- [Yangrak] Daughter?
- So I am.

114
00:04:23,555 --> 00:04:24,638
YUN SUYEON

115
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:26,390
AGE 21, YUN IGYEONG'S DAUGHTER

116
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,392
[Pani Bottle] Bokgil is a slave.

117
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:30,352
- I'm a slave?
- [Jiyoon] Yes.

118
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:31,563
[others laugh]

119
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:35,566
BOKGIL

120
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:36,776
AGE 25, YUN IGYEONG'S SLAVE

121
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:39,236
[Pani Bottle] Musoe is a maid.

122
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,697
- [gasps] Oh, Musoe's a woman!
- [Sungrok] It's a female character.

123
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:43,240
- [Yangrak] She's a maid.
- It's a woman.

124
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:44,242
[Jiyoon] She's Suyeon's maid.

125
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:50,080
MUSOE

126
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:51,874
AGE 21, YUN SUYEON'S MAID

127
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:53,250
[Jiyoon] The Traveler is an outsider.

128
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:54,627
[Pani Bottle] His identity's unknown.

129
00:04:54,628 --> 00:04:56,546
"A rare air of nobility
in this mountain village."

130
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,593
THE TRAVELER

131
00:05:02,594 --> 00:05:04,845
AGE 43, MYSTERIOUS IDENTITY

132
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,597
FATHER AND DAUGHTER
SLAVE, MAID

133
00:05:06,598 --> 00:05:08,182
TRAVELER

134
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:10,351
[host] <i>The second story
of</i> Murder Club <i>will now begin.</i>

135
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:13,938
<i>"Gwandong Byeolgok:
The Exile Murder Case."</i>

136
00:05:13,939 --> 00:05:15,857
Gwandong Byeolgok?

137
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:20,737
[narrator] <i>Despite the spread of famine
across the eight provinces of Joseon,</i>

138
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:25,242
<i>the king demanded a raise in taxes.</i>

139
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:28,494
<i>Yun Igyeong, a local official,</i>

140
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:30,913
<i>saw the people's suffering</i>

141
00:05:30,914 --> 00:05:34,584
<i>and submitted a petition
opposing the tax reform.</i>

142
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:40,005
<i>His petition angered the king</i>

143
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:44,177
<i>and Yun Igyeong ended up in exile.</i>

144
00:05:44,845 --> 00:05:49,181
<i>With his only daughter, Yun Suyeon,
and her maid, Musoe,</i>

145
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:51,475
<i>he began a life in exile</i>

146
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:56,439
<i>with the help of Bokgil,
a slave he met there.</i>

147
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:58,691
<i>Then one day,</i>

148
00:05:58,692 --> 00:06:03,237
<i>a traveler he'd never met before
asked to stay the night.</i>

149
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:07,992
<i>Late in the night,
as the five people got ready for bed,</i>

150
00:06:07,993 --> 00:06:10,953
<i>the incident took place.</i>

151
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:14,915
<i>The next morning,
Musoe went into the back yard</i>

152
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:19,713
<i>and found an unidentified dead body
with a disfigured face.</i>

153
00:06:20,547 --> 00:06:23,174
[host] <i>Here is the first shared clue.</i>

154
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:26,176
[Bokgil] Oh, goodness.

155
00:06:26,177 --> 00:06:29,096
- Their face is completely disfigured.
- [Suyeon gasps]

156
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:31,599
It looks like it was torn by a wild beast.

157
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,559
- Is it a man or a woman?
- [Bokgil groans]

158
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,603
They're too disfigured to tell.

159
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:36,854
[The Traveler] I think it's a man.

160
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:38,064
They're wearing pants.

161
00:06:38,732 --> 00:06:41,818
[host] <i>Pick the card clues for Round 1.</i>

162
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:47,323
<i>Every player has
a total of five card clues.</i>

163
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:52,244
<i>Each card contains a secret
that no other player knows.</i>

164
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:55,998
<i>In every round except for the fifth round,</i>

165
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:59,501
<i>the players can take one card
from the person they suspect.</i>

166
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:03,340
<i>Use the collected clues
to determine who the culprit is.</i>

167
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,633
- We can pick any, right?
- That's right.

168
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:07,302
I'll take one of my dad's.

169
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:08,970
I'll go for this one.

170
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:13,600
Okay, then. Me too.

171
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:16,769
[Suyeon] You've lost two cards.

172
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,314
The Traveler is obviously
the most suspicious.

173
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,067
I'll take one from here.

174
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:24,736
- [Bokgil] Musoe's card.
- One of Musoe's cards.

175
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:28,656
You're a bit far,
but I've been doubting you, lady.

176
00:07:28,657 --> 00:07:30,949
[Suyeon] How could you doubt me
after all these years?

177
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,744
THE PLAYERS CAN SHARE
WHAT THEY KNOW FROM THE CARD CLUES

178
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:36,997
BUT THEY CAN ONLY SHOW THE ACTUAL CARD
DURING PRIVATE CONVERSATIONS

179
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:40,292
<i>-It's time to collect the object clues.</i>
- [Suyeon] Okay. Let's go.

180
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:42,379
[Igyeong] Let's see what we have.

181
00:07:44,047 --> 00:07:46,048
EVIDENCE ZONE

182
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:48,342
EACH PLAYER MAY COLLECT
1 OBJECT CLUE PER ROUND

183
00:07:48,343 --> 00:07:49,802
THE OWNER OF THE CLUE IS UNSPECIFIED

184
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:51,388
- I'm taking this one.
- [Bokgil] Which one?

185
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:58,560
[host] <i>Round 1 will now begin.</i>

186
00:07:58,561 --> 00:08:01,063
Are we now in the Joseon era?

187
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:02,856
Shall we talk like people in the old days?

188
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,275
ANXIOUS ABOUT BEING
LAST IN THE PECKING ORDER

189
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:06,568
Hey, Bokgil!

190
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,696
- Bokgil!
- Why, you little…

191
00:08:08,697 --> 00:08:09,780
What?

192
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:11,573
- "You little"?
- Wait. You were a lord?

193
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:13,617
- How dare you, you lowly slave?
- [Igyeong] The nerve…

194
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:15,285
My ears must be deceiving me.

195
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:16,453
Why, of course.

196
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:18,080
BACKING DOWN

197
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:20,749
Bokgil looks a lot older than his age.

198
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,836
- He's worked too hard.
- [Igyeong] He's had a tough life.

199
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:24,712
What is that in your hand, Suyeon?

200
00:08:24,713 --> 00:08:27,966
Father, this is
a bloodstained handkerchief.

201
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:30,676
ROUND 1 OBJECT CLUE:
BLOODSTAINED HANDKERCHIEF

202
00:08:30,677 --> 00:08:34,054
Seeing how elegant the embroidery is,

203
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:36,473
I think it likely
belongs to someone noble.

204
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:40,352
People like me and Bokgil
could not use such a handkerchief.

205
00:08:40,353 --> 00:08:42,647
Bokgil has always had

206
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,607
rather sticky fingers.

207
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:46,775
It's a baseless accusation.

208
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,444
You're saying Bokgil stole it?

209
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:50,362
What kind of slave
wears a watch like this?

210
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:52,197
- [Igyeong] Wait a minute.
- No, no.

211
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:54,242
- What is this, Bokgil?
- [Suyeon] You stole it, didn't you?

212
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:56,618
[Bokgil] Let's see. Object number 14.

213
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,287
WHAT OBJECT CLUE DID BOKGIL BRING?

214
00:08:58,288 --> 00:08:59,663
ROUND 1 OBJECT CLUE: RASPBERRIES

215
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:01,707
- [Igyeong] Raspberries?
- [Bokgil] Yes, raspberries.

216
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:03,042
Try one, Bokgil.

217
00:09:03,043 --> 00:09:04,376
You go first.

218
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:05,544
What did you say?

219
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:07,087
- [others chuckle]
- How dare you!

220
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:08,839
[stammers] Oh, right. Noble lady.

221
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,507
- I forgot.
- Why, this little…

222
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:11,967
This is all a bit…

223
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:13,093
STRUGGLING TO ADJUST

224
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:15,013
It's outright insubordination!

225
00:09:16,222 --> 00:09:17,681
[Igyeong] You shouldn't eat that.

226
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:19,184
It's definitely a raspberry.

227
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:23,313
[Bokgil] But what can raspberries prove?

228
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:26,065
I found a silver dagger.

229
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:27,149
[Bokgil] A silver dagger?

230
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:28,984
There's blood on it.

231
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:30,819
Don't women carry them around

232
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,654
- to protect themselves?
- Ladies usually

233
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:35,241
carry it for self-defense.

234
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:37,743
Why would you do such a thing, my lady?

235
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:40,162
But Musoe just now…

236
00:09:40,163 --> 00:09:42,456
She shouldn't have ever
laid hands on one before,

237
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:45,918
but she suspiciously
whipped it out like a seasoned pro.

238
00:09:45,919 --> 00:09:47,419
It has iron in it, doesn't it?

239
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,505
WHOSE SILVER DAGGER IS IT?

240
00:09:49,506 --> 00:09:50,757
Let's look at what I brought.

241
00:09:51,508 --> 00:09:53,258
ROUND 1 OBJECT CLUE: SILK CLOTHES

242
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,343
[all gasp]

243
00:09:54,344 --> 00:09:55,844
- Silk clothing.
- [Bokgil] It's conclusive proof.

244
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:57,513
It's some fancy hanbok.

245
00:09:57,514 --> 00:09:58,847
[Suyeon] It's a rich man's clothes.

246
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:00,391
It looks like the Traveler's size.

247
00:10:01,935 --> 00:10:04,604
[The Traveler] A passing traveler couldn't
wear such fancy clothes.

248
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:07,439
But who are you, by the way?

249
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,233
I'm just passing through.

250
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:10,276
A wandering traveler.

251
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:12,111
Usually, travelers

252
00:10:12,112 --> 00:10:13,987
- have dirty faces…
- That's right.

253
00:10:13,988 --> 00:10:16,074
…and tattered clothes.

254
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:20,410
- But he's too dashing.
- His looks aren't of an ordinary traveler.

255
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:22,955
- What's your object clue?
- [Bokgil] Your clothes aren't…

256
00:10:22,956 --> 00:10:25,415
- What's that?
- [The Traveler] It's an herbal tonic.

257
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:28,127
<i>"Arsenic, chive seeds, wolfsbane</i>…<i>"</i>

258
00:10:28,128 --> 00:10:29,253
[Bokgil] <i>Oh, that means…</i>

259
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:31,380
- [Suyeon] Is it poison?
-…it's a poison.

260
00:10:31,381 --> 00:10:33,090
Give it a taste, Bokgil.

261
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:35,134
WHY DO YOU KEEP TELLING ME TO TASTE…

262
00:10:35,135 --> 00:10:37,636
- She's treating you like a mutt, Bokgil.
- [others laugh]

263
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:38,929
[Bokgil] That's poison. Don't eat that!

264
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:41,515
- Come on, Bokgil.
- No, thank you.

265
00:10:41,516 --> 00:10:44,560
How could a lowly man like me drink that?

266
00:10:44,561 --> 00:10:46,186
But if they fed the victim poison,

267
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:47,813
the poison would have killed them.

268
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:50,065
So why did they disfigure their face?

269
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:51,317
It seems like the victim

270
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:53,443
was slashed by a blade,

271
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:55,320
and more notably,

272
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:58,490
they have a blue bruise
on the back of their hand.

273
00:10:58,491 --> 00:11:00,450
Maybe they tried to shield themselves.

274
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:02,494
- They were struck.
- It's a possibility.

275
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:05,873
[Igyeong] That long slash across the chest
looks like a blade wound.

276
00:11:05,874 --> 00:11:08,041
You can't do that with a silver dagger.

277
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:11,962
- [Bokgil] Of course, not.
- It would only leave a small cut.

278
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:14,089
It had to be a long blade

279
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:16,925
handled by someone skilled in combat.

280
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:19,970
His face is mangled.

281
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:22,222
And it seems like he was
dragged across the ground.

282
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:25,893
Maybe he had a really handsome face,

283
00:11:25,894 --> 00:11:27,896
so he was targeted by someone

284
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:29,939
who had reason to envy him.

285
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:33,443
- Why did she look at us two?
- [others chuckle]

286
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:35,903
I didn't mean anything by it, Father.

287
00:11:35,904 --> 00:11:37,739
Why look at us two, of all people?

288
00:11:38,907 --> 00:11:40,407
[Igyeong] The cards we picked earlier…

289
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,075
- [Suyeon] You mean this?
- [Bokgil] The ones we picked.

290
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:43,285
Whose was it?

291
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:44,620
I took it from my father.

292
00:11:44,621 --> 00:11:46,872
- It's Yun Igyeong's card.
- You suspect your father.

293
00:11:46,873 --> 00:11:49,583
There was a note in his pillow.

294
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:51,376
It said, "Don't make any moves,"

295
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:53,420
in the sense of keeping a low profile.

296
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,214
It seems political.

297
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:56,423
INFO FROM THE KING'S COURT?

298
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:57,716
Was something going on?

299
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:59,259
Something political?

300
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:02,012
- I can't tell you.
- [Bokgil] It's because of politics

301
00:12:02,013 --> 00:12:03,931
that he was exiled.

302
00:12:03,932 --> 00:12:05,265
Politically speaking,

303
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:07,976
whether he was framed or actually guilty,

304
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,645
he's considered a criminal.

305
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:11,146
You're very smart, Bokgil.

306
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:13,691
[Suyeon] Why would someone send
this note to a criminal?

307
00:12:14,317 --> 00:12:16,401
SNEAKING A PEEK

308
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:19,279
- How dare you sneak a peek!
- [others chuckle]

309
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:21,240
So this is the kind of sly trick

310
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:23,742
- you have up your sleeve.
- No.

311
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:26,037
You're the only one here
wearing magnifying glasses.

312
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:29,206
I also obtained a clue.

313
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,707
- Go on, Dad.
- I took a card

314
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:33,585
- from the passing traveler
- [The Traveler] "Dad."

315
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:35,879
and it was a list of books.

316
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,214
- A list of books.
- Okay.

317
00:12:37,215 --> 00:12:39,466
<i>Was it</i> The Analects?
<i>I'm not good with Chinese characters.</i>

318
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,260
[Bokgil] The Analects? <i>That means…</i>

319
00:12:41,261 --> 00:12:45,180
[Igyeong] It's a bit advanced
for an ordinary traveler.

320
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,391
- He's a learned traveler.
- Yeah, if he's reading <i>The Analects</i>.

321
00:12:47,392 --> 00:12:48,892
He's reading Confucian Classics.

322
00:12:48,893 --> 00:12:51,436
Not a lot of people can read,

323
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:53,063
I can't even spell my name.

324
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:54,481
And it's just two words, "Bok Gili."

325
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:55,899
Your name is "Bok Gili"?

326
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,986
- Not just Bokgil?
- [Igyeong] Is Bok a surname?

327
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,445
- Your name's just "Gil"?
- Which Bok clan is it?

328
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:02,322
I don't even know that much.

329
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:05,284
But why did you have
<i>The Analects</i> in your bag?

330
00:13:05,285 --> 00:13:08,078
[The Traveler]
You can learn that much anywhere.

331
00:13:08,079 --> 00:13:10,456
I picked a witness testimony.

332
00:13:10,957 --> 00:13:12,500
The Traveler,

333
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,252
judging by his appearance,

334
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:17,254
<i>doesn't seem like a commoner</i>

335
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:20,215
<i>but a very high-ranking person.</i>

336
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,967
What are you doing in this village?

337
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:24,261
- Why my house, of all places?
- [Bokgil] Where were you headed?

338
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:25,345
It is very suspicious.

339
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:26,471
[Suyeon] Who told him we had room?

340
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,765
- [Bokgil] He's the most suspicious.
- [Suyeon] It wasn't me.

341
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:30,435
[Bokgil] Where were you headed?

342
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:32,811
He wasn't with us before.

343
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:35,397
He appeared out of the blue
on the very day of the murder.

344
00:13:35,398 --> 00:13:36,940
Within 24 hours.

345
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:40,027
I feel like he is the most likely suspect.

346
00:13:40,028 --> 00:13:42,070
[host] <i>Round 1 is over.</i>

347
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,655
We didn't get to discuss everything.

348
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:45,407
Musoe didn't even get a chance to talk.

349
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:46,576
Come on, man!

350
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:48,326
ROUND 1 CARD CLUES

351
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:50,912
PILLOW NOTE, TRAVELER'S BAG,
VILLAGE ELDER'S WITNESS STATEMENT

352
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:52,707
[host] <i>Here is a new shared clue.</i>

353
00:13:53,458 --> 00:13:55,792
BLUEPRINT OF THE EXILE GROUNDS

354
00:13:55,793 --> 00:13:56,794
Hang on!

355
00:13:57,295 --> 00:13:58,712
There's a trail of blood.

356
00:13:58,713 --> 00:14:00,380
A TRAIL OF BLOOD
SHOWING THE KILLER'S ROUTE

357
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,507
- This was…
- I see.

358
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:04,384
The guest room, kitchen,

359
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:05,802
Yun Igyeong's room, and the main hall.

360
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:07,054
That's the route.

361
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,638
This shows Musoe and I are innocent.

362
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:10,307
Same for me.

363
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:11,892
- Yeah, Bokgil too.
- That means…

364
00:14:11,893 --> 00:14:13,185
Thank you, my lady.

365
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:15,228
FULLY IMMERSED IN HIS ROLE

366
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:17,982
This narrows it down
to the Traveler and Yun Igyeong.

367
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:19,775
[Suyeon] The route is a little odd.

368
00:14:19,776 --> 00:14:21,069
[Bokgil] Just based on this.

369
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:24,529
[host] <i>Pick the card clues for Round 2.</i>

370
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,073
[Bokgil] Give me one.

371
00:14:26,074 --> 00:14:27,240
BOKGIL TAKES A CARD FROM MUSOE

372
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:28,408
What's my daughter been up to?

373
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:30,244
We haven't talked much
since you hit puberty.

374
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:32,580
YUN IGYEONG TAKES A CARD FROM YUN SUYEON

375
00:14:33,915 --> 00:14:37,584
- Now you're suspecting me?
- [The Traveler sighs]

376
00:14:37,585 --> 00:14:39,795
I find you suspicious, sir.

377
00:14:39,796 --> 00:14:41,922
MUSOE TAKES A CARD FROM YUN IGYEONG

378
00:14:41,923 --> 00:14:44,591
I find you suspicious, Mr. Traveler.

379
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:47,094
YUN SUYEON TAKES A CARD FROM THE TRAVELER

380
00:14:47,095 --> 00:14:49,721
[host] <i>Head over to the evidence zone</i>

381
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:52,182
<i>and collect object clues.</i>

382
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:53,643
I'll just take this bundle.

383
00:14:55,478 --> 00:14:56,938
What's this?

384
00:14:58,606 --> 00:14:59,689
[Igyeong] You go first, Musoe.

385
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:00,774
ROUND 2

386
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:02,526
[Musoe] It's someone's belongings.

387
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:04,778
- [Suyeon] Belongings?
- [Musoe] And shoes.

388
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:06,280
[Igyeong] Whose is it?

389
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:07,865
[Suyeon] Wait a minute.

390
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:10,326
Bokgil, you scoundrel!

391
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:13,662
That's your personal color, isn't it?

392
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:16,748
What are my clothes doing in there?

393
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,792
- Wait. What's that?
- [all exclaim]

394
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:20,502
- [Bokgil] What's that?
- [Suyeon] What is it?

395
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:22,712
- [Suyeon] A hairpin?
- That's so random.

396
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,005
[Igyeong] But these are men's clothes.

397
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:25,549
WHAT DOES THE NOTE SAY?

398
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:26,633
[The Traveler] Well?

399
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:29,010
[Musoe] "Forgive my boldness,

400
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:32,055
but can I spend
the rest of my life by your side?"

401
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:33,181
That's what it says.

402
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,517
IT SEEMS LIKE A MARRIAGE PROPOSAL

403
00:15:35,518 --> 00:15:37,644
- Isn't it a love letter?
- [Musoe] Yeah.

404
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:40,188
[The Traveler] Bokgil was
in love with you, my lady.

405
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,232
- [Bokgil] No. It was Musoe.
- [The Traveler] Was it mutual?

406
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:43,316
COULD IT BE?

407
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,069
I think Bokgil

408
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:48,071
stole my hairpin

409
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,990
and planned to run away with Musoe.

410
00:15:49,991 --> 00:15:51,074
BLUSH

411
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:52,160
[Igyeong] Lovers fleeing at night?

412
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,452
But who wrote that note?

413
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:56,496
- It must have been you.
- Me?

414
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:58,958
But I can't even spell own my name.

415
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:02,002
- [Bokgil] Come on.
- Let's examine my object clue.

416
00:16:02,003 --> 00:16:03,588
A hair comb?

417
00:16:04,255 --> 00:16:06,006
- [Suyeon] It's a fine-tooth comb.
- Yeah.

418
00:16:06,007 --> 00:16:07,549
[Igyeong] It's women's clothing.

419
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,260
A WOMAN'S BELONGINGS

420
00:16:10,428 --> 00:16:11,429
A ring? There are two!

421
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:14,556
- [Suyeon] The hairpin earlier--
- Wedding rings?

422
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:15,849
[Musoe] <i>Don't they seem like Suyeon's?</i>

423
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:16,933
It looks like

424
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:20,729
when two people pack their belongings
to run away together.

425
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:22,564
A MAN'S BELONGINGS
WITH A PROPOSAL FOR MARRIAGE

426
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:26,276
AND A WOMAN'S BELONGINGS
WITH WEDDING RINGS

427
00:16:26,277 --> 00:16:29,946
But since they're jade rings,
I think they belong to the lady.

428
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:32,074
They're yours, my lady.

429
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:34,242
[Musoe] I couldn't own a jade ring.

430
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:35,577
You two stole them from me.

431
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:37,663
HOW MANY THIEVES ARE IN THIS HOUSEHOLD?

432
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:39,581
We're not catching thieves,

433
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:41,708
we're looking for the murderer.

434
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,878
They were actually my belongings.

435
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:45,587
I packed them.

436
00:16:45,588 --> 00:16:50,300
I'll be in big trouble if they found out
about my relations with Bokgil.

437
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:52,553
I don't want anyone to know about it.

438
00:16:53,596 --> 00:16:56,556
WERE THEY LOVERS?

439
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:59,392
Why did you two steal all my stuff?

440
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:00,977
SIGH

441
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:03,230
Something's always missing
whenever I get back home.

442
00:17:03,231 --> 00:17:05,065
- Where did you get that ring?
- [others chuckle]

443
00:17:05,066 --> 00:17:07,359
- It's mine, isn't it?
- [Bokgil] No, my lady.

444
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,860
Ms. Paeng gave it to me.

445
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:10,153
"Ms. Paeng."

446
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:11,238
Wait. Who is Ms. Paeng?

447
00:17:11,239 --> 00:17:13,282
- Who's Ms. Paeng?
- [Igyeong] Who is that?

448
00:17:14,325 --> 00:17:15,659
Bring out the sword.

449
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:17,118
This is key evidence. Look here.

450
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:19,746
Is there blood on it?

451
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:21,164
Right, this sword here…

452
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,958
- [Bokgil] Be careful.
-…is huge.

453
00:17:22,959 --> 00:17:25,043
- [Bokgil] Gosh.
- [The Traveler] Wow.

454
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:26,670
But as for any bloodstains…

455
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:28,797
- [Bokgil] Are there any?
- It looks clean.

456
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:30,090
They must have wiped it.

457
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:31,508
They tried for a perfect murder.

458
00:17:31,509 --> 00:17:32,801
- [gasps]
- The murder weapon, the silver dagger…

459
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:34,178
What is it?

460
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:38,974
Earlier, my handkerchief
was soaked with blood, right?

461
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:40,809
<i>They must have used it to wipe this sword.</i>

462
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:42,435
HANDKERCHIEF USED TO WIPE THE BLOOD?

463
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:43,688
- Father!
- [Bokgil chuckles]

464
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,647
Why is that mine?

465
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:47,983
It's either yours or the Traveler's.

466
00:17:47,984 --> 00:17:51,361
If you put the sword
and the handkerchief together,

467
00:17:51,362 --> 00:17:55,323
"wealthy" and "male"
are the words that come to mind.

468
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:57,117
<i>Two people fit that description.</i>

469
00:17:57,118 --> 00:17:59,537
<i>I don't want to believe it,
but one is my father.</i>

470
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:01,914
<i>The other is the Traveler.</i>

471
00:18:03,249 --> 00:18:07,002
WHOSE HANDKERCHIEF AND SWORD IS IT?

472
00:18:07,003 --> 00:18:09,087
Before we solve this,

473
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,590
the card I picked said

474
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:12,675
that Bokgil

475
00:18:13,593 --> 00:18:14,676
brewed tonics.

476
00:18:14,677 --> 00:18:16,177
TRACES OF SECRETLY BREWED TONICS

477
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,304
There were traces.

478
00:18:17,305 --> 00:18:18,306
Tonic?

479
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:22,809
DID BOKGIL BREW TONICS
ON THE LOCAL MOUNTAIN?

480
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,228
You are the absolute worst, Bokgil.

481
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:26,229
I am innocent, my lady.

482
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,689
- You're up to all sorts.
- No, listen.

483
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:29,357
Every morning and night…

484
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,568
- The type of tonic is what matters.
- [Bokgil] Exactly.

485
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:33,612
But that tonic before

486
00:18:33,613 --> 00:18:36,656
<i>was a poison, as we saw earlier.</i>

487
00:18:36,657 --> 00:18:38,325
[Bokgil]
I don't know anything about poisons.

488
00:18:38,326 --> 00:18:39,701
Where would I get that?

489
00:18:39,702 --> 00:18:41,411
- Where do they sell poison?
- [Igyeong] He's dangerous.

490
00:18:41,412 --> 00:18:43,705
- He's a dangerous man.
- [Bokgil] Gosh.

491
00:18:43,706 --> 00:18:46,374
Bokgil keeps insisting it wasn't him.

492
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:49,294
I don't know exactly

493
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:51,379
who he secretly brewed the tonic for,

494
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,757
but I think he's hiding something.

495
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:56,718
I'm sorry to interrupt,
but this is really important.

496
00:18:56,719 --> 00:19:00,013
The blue mark on the wrist
of the dead victim isn't a bruise.

497
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:01,891
They were born with that mark.

498
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:03,600
- It's a birth mark?
- [Igyeong] Yeah.

499
00:19:03,601 --> 00:19:05,560
- It's a kind of mole?
- I mention this because

500
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:08,229
on my daughter's bookshelf,

501
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,483
there's a Birth Chamber Log that mentions

502
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:14,695
a newborn baby with a mark
on the back of their right hand.

503
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:20,408
A BABY BORN WITH A BLUE MARK
ON THE BACK OF ITS HAND?

504
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:22,494
But why was that record
in my daughter's room?

505
00:19:22,495 --> 00:19:24,746
Does that mean Lady Suyeon had a child?

506
00:19:24,747 --> 00:19:27,374
What nonsense!

507
00:19:27,375 --> 00:19:29,125
She's an unmarried woman.

508
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:30,335
How could you suggest that?

509
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,961
- Out of the blue.
- What an accusation.

510
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:35,882
Wait. I didn't get to share
my card clue in Round 1, right?

511
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:37,634
NERVOUS

512
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:40,888
But Lady Suyeon wrote,
"I didn't menstruate."

513
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:43,139
What? Oh.

514
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,432
So she was pregnant?

515
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:46,601
- Unbelievable.
- The record I found was about births.

516
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,686
It was a delivery log.

517
00:19:47,687 --> 00:19:50,271
So it could be her child.

518
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:51,690
But Suyeon's still…

519
00:19:51,691 --> 00:19:54,067
The victim's too old to be her child.

520
00:19:54,068 --> 00:19:55,735
- We look about the same age.
- [Igyeong] Can you imagine?

521
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:57,445
- [The Traveler] How old are you?
- The victim looks older.

522
00:19:57,446 --> 00:19:58,863
Reveal your age!

523
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:02,033
I'm just 21 years old, you bastards!

524
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:04,661
- Did I have a child when I was two?
- Then this guy…

525
00:20:04,662 --> 00:20:07,622
She'd have to give birth
before she was even born.

526
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:10,042
- He looks older than me.
- She gave birth in the womb.

527
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:12,460
Another possibility is

528
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:15,213
that the victim's son

529
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:17,132
had the same birthmark,

530
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:18,758
or something like that.

531
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:20,385
It's another possibility.

532
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:23,304
The Birth Chamber Log is pretty major.

533
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:25,390
How did that come out as evidence?

534
00:20:25,391 --> 00:20:28,101
WHAT SECRET IS SUYEON HIDING?

535
00:20:28,102 --> 00:20:30,979
[host] <i>Starting Round 2,
the private conversation zones are open.</i>

536
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:35,483
<i>Anyone who wants a private conversation
can freely access this zone.</i>

537
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:38,236
I never doubted you, my lord.

538
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:40,989
The person I suspect is none other

539
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:42,073
than Suyeon.

540
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:43,950
- Because right now--
- Your own daughter?

541
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:45,368
She has too many secrets.

542
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:47,746
- The birth record we discussed earlier
- Yes.

543
00:20:47,747 --> 00:20:51,500
<i>and the blue mark
on the victim's right hand</i>…

544
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,377
There's a lot I don't know
about my own daughter.

545
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:55,795
She has a lot of secrets.

546
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,715
You seem to have some connection

547
00:20:58,424 --> 00:21:00,467
to the dead victim.

548
00:21:00,468 --> 00:21:02,510
I don't know them at all.

549
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:05,221
- The birth record.
- Yeah.

550
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:08,016
It seems like you have a secret.

551
00:21:08,017 --> 00:21:09,560
I've never seen it before.

552
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:12,562
I have no idea why it was in my room.

553
00:21:12,563 --> 00:21:14,731
You are obviously hiding something.

554
00:21:14,732 --> 00:21:18,193
But both the cards I picked

555
00:21:18,194 --> 00:21:20,570
mention a dark rumor circulating at court

556
00:21:20,571 --> 00:21:23,698
and warned you to be on your guard.

557
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,159
- Mmm.
- So here's what I suspect.

558
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:29,245
The victim tried to get you,

559
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:32,916
so you eliminated him first.

560
00:21:32,917 --> 00:21:34,083
WAS THE TRAVELER IN DANGER?

561
00:21:34,084 --> 00:21:37,587
I'm only telling you two
since we're having a private conversation.

562
00:21:37,588 --> 00:21:38,880
The truth is,

563
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:41,801
the reason for my lavish attire

564
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:44,302
is because I'm Grand Prince Hwiryeong.

565
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:46,137
- Grand Prince Hwiryeong?
- Grand Prince Hwiryeong?

566
00:21:46,138 --> 00:21:48,848
- I'm the king's younger brother.
- [Musoe gasps]

567
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:51,101
[announcer]
Here comes the Grand Prince Hwiryeong!

568
00:21:57,608 --> 00:21:58,691
GRAND PRINCE HWIRYEONG

569
00:21:58,692 --> 00:22:00,985
KING'S YOUNGER BROTHER,
PLANS TO USURP THE THRONE

570
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:03,404
If I keep hiding my identity,

571
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:06,324
they could mistake me for the killer.

572
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,785
So I had no choice

573
00:22:08,494 --> 00:22:09,870
but to reveal some of the truth.

574
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:14,082
THE TRAVELER'S IDENTITY
IS FINALLY REVEALED

575
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:16,125
Gosh. High Prince.

576
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:17,502
Grand Prince.

577
00:22:17,503 --> 00:22:18,962
- Right, Grand Prince. [chuckles]
- Grand Prince.

578
00:22:18,963 --> 00:22:20,255
Do you understand now?

579
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:21,798
Please have mercy.

580
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:23,675
But why did you kill someone,
Your Highness?

581
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:25,468
I did not kill them.

582
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:28,304
I heard that Yun Igyeong

583
00:22:28,305 --> 00:22:31,307
had fallen on hard times.

584
00:22:31,308 --> 00:22:32,725
So I disguised myself as a traveler--

585
00:22:32,726 --> 00:22:34,477
- You came to help?
- I came to help.

586
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:35,979
But why hide your identity?

587
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:37,772
If I didn't adopt this disguise,

588
00:22:37,773 --> 00:22:40,275
- I could become a target of assassins.
- Mmm.

589
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:42,068
So I had to keep my identity a secret.

590
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:44,028
- Like secret royal inspectors.
- Exactly.

591
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,822
He said he was the Grand Prince Hwiryeong,

592
00:22:45,823 --> 00:22:49,701
so I'm convinced something went down
between him and Lord Yun.

593
00:22:49,702 --> 00:22:51,494
<i>Since he's been exiled,</i>

594
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:54,664
<i>he might be planning
a revolt with the grand prince.</i>

595
00:22:54,665 --> 00:22:56,833
Or their close relationship

596
00:22:56,834 --> 00:23:00,254
might be the reason
he was exiled in the first place.

597
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:03,548
ARE THEY ALLIES?

598
00:23:03,549 --> 00:23:05,300
[host]
<i>Here is the shared clue for Round 3.</i>

599
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:07,553
<i>It's an audio of the murder incident.</i>

600
00:23:08,137 --> 00:23:10,138
DOOR OPENING

601
00:23:10,139 --> 00:23:14,642
- [door closes]
- [footsteps approaching]

602
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:16,561
SHATTERING

603
00:23:16,562 --> 00:23:17,729
[sword unsheathes]

604
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:18,813
A SLASHING SWORD

605
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:22,526
[sword swishes]

606
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:25,653
LIMPING

607
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:29,741
- [footsteps]
- [door opens and closes]

608
00:23:29,742 --> 00:23:30,825
SLASHING SWORD 2

609
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:33,161
- [liquid spills]
- [victim breathing heavily]

610
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:34,038
[thuds]

611
00:23:35,581 --> 00:23:37,249
[door opens]

612
00:23:38,042 --> 00:23:42,128
DRAGGING

613
00:23:42,129 --> 00:23:43,546
Is that the corpse being dragged?

614
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:45,173
[footsteps running]

615
00:23:45,174 --> 00:23:46,215
FLEEING

616
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,217
[door closes]

617
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,469
That's brutal.

618
00:23:49,470 --> 00:23:51,262
There were two sword sounds, right?

619
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:55,601
But there was no scream
when the sword was first swung.

620
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:57,644
There was a scream the second time.

621
00:23:57,645 --> 00:23:58,937
A swing and a miss.

622
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:01,397
- First it felt like practice.
- Like it was forced.

623
00:24:01,398 --> 00:24:02,982
But only one person died, right?

624
00:24:02,983 --> 00:24:04,693
- Not two?
- [Bokgil] Just one person.

625
00:24:05,194 --> 00:24:07,362
[host] <i>Pick out the card clues.</i>

626
00:24:07,363 --> 00:24:08,529
TIME TO SELECT CARD CLUES

627
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:10,740
THE TRAVELER TAKES ONE FROM MUSOE

628
00:24:10,741 --> 00:24:12,951
MUSOE TAKES ONE FROM YUN IGYEONG

629
00:24:12,952 --> 00:24:15,370
YUN SUYEON TAKES ONE FROM BOKGIL

630
00:24:15,371 --> 00:24:17,789
YUN IGYEONG TAKES ONE FROM YUN SUYEON

631
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:20,291
BOKGIL TAKES ONE FROM MUSOE

632
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:23,128
[Suyeon sighs]
The object clues are low-key important.

633
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:27,216
All right. Let's take this one.

634
00:24:30,427 --> 00:24:32,887
[host] <i>Round 3 will now begin.</i>

635
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:35,057
Did this heart symbol exist
in the Joseon era?

636
00:24:35,641 --> 00:24:37,183
ROUND 3 OBJECT CLUE: A LOVE NOTE

637
00:24:37,184 --> 00:24:38,351
MY LOVE, BOKGIL

638
00:24:38,352 --> 00:24:39,602
[Suyeon] "My love, Bokgil."

639
00:24:39,603 --> 00:24:40,770
MUSOE

640
00:24:40,771 --> 00:24:41,772
"Musoe"?

641
00:24:42,690 --> 00:24:43,856
What the heck?

642
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:46,317
WHAT'S THE STORY BEHIND THIS?

643
00:24:46,318 --> 00:24:49,195
I think it's true that Musoe liked me.

644
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:51,197
IS SUYEON JEALOUS?

645
00:24:51,198 --> 00:24:53,701
To be honest, since Bokgil first moved in,

646
00:24:54,368 --> 00:24:56,786
- I couldn't take my eyes off him.
- How mortifying.

647
00:24:56,787 --> 00:24:59,872
MUSOE BRAVELY CONFESSES HER FEELINGS

648
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:01,250
[♪ romantic music playing]

649
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:07,423
[heartbeat thumping]

650
00:25:09,425 --> 00:25:12,135
LOVE TRIANGLE
YUN SUYEON, BOKGIL, MUSOE

651
00:25:12,136 --> 00:25:15,013
How mortifying.
Flirting under someone else's roof.

652
00:25:15,014 --> 00:25:16,514
Musoe, you little…

653
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:18,641
What were you doing yesterday night?

654
00:25:18,642 --> 00:25:20,601
- [Bokgil] Yeah, what were you doing?
- Last night?

655
00:25:20,602 --> 00:25:21,937
I actually heard

656
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:25,399
Bokgil and Lady Yun
planned to run away together.

657
00:25:25,983 --> 00:25:28,026
What are you on about?
I was asleep in my room.

658
00:25:28,027 --> 00:25:29,819
That's not true, my lady.

659
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:32,405
- [others laugh]
- I think we've been caught.

660
00:25:32,406 --> 00:25:33,740
What are you talking about?

661
00:25:33,741 --> 00:25:36,534
Why deny it now?

662
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:39,579
I noticed he looked at you
in an unusual way.

663
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:41,873
He just has weird eyes.

664
00:25:41,874 --> 00:25:43,916
- Your taste is men is even weirder.
- [others laugh]

665
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:46,003
- [Musoe] So…
- Oh man, Bokgil.

666
00:25:47,171 --> 00:25:50,924
I have never in my life
dated a guy with sideburns.

667
00:25:51,467 --> 00:25:53,176
- - You were saying?
- So

668
00:25:53,177 --> 00:25:56,054
after hearing you'd flee in the night,
I couldn't sleep.

669
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:58,723
so I went into the kitchen
to pack you some extra food,

670
00:25:58,724 --> 00:26:00,892
like raspberries.

671
00:26:00,893 --> 00:26:02,894
<i>-That's what those raspberries were for.
-</i> [Bokgil] <i>Ah.</i>

672
00:26:02,895 --> 00:26:04,021
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

673
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:06,814
I think that could be a lie

674
00:26:06,815 --> 00:26:09,567
because Musoe loves Bokgil,

675
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:12,028
so why would she pack raspberries
for you to flee together?

676
00:26:12,029 --> 00:26:14,447
- It makes no sense.
- [Igyeong] It's odd.

677
00:26:14,448 --> 00:26:16,866
I think it's a mix of lie and truth.

678
00:26:16,867 --> 00:26:18,367
Did you plan to flee in the night?

679
00:26:18,368 --> 00:26:20,037
No, Dad.

680
00:26:21,455 --> 00:26:22,663
- It is true, sir.
- [others laugh]

681
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:24,333
Who's telling the truth?

682
00:26:24,833 --> 00:26:26,375
[Igyeong]
Are you ashamed of your boyfriend?

683
00:26:26,376 --> 00:26:29,587
What were you doing yesterday night?

684
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:31,380
I'll explain what happened.

685
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:32,590
- Tell the truth.
- Explain.

686
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:33,674
To be honest,

687
00:26:33,675 --> 00:26:36,428
Bokgil was just a one-night stand.

688
00:26:37,012 --> 00:26:38,846
A one-night stand? What's that?

689
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:40,932
I don't really love him, I just--

690
00:26:40,933 --> 00:26:42,391
You said you did!

691
00:26:42,392 --> 00:26:44,102
It was just pillow talk.

692
00:26:44,103 --> 00:26:45,603
You said I was just your type!

693
00:26:45,604 --> 00:26:47,688
- I was just talking about your body.
- [others laugh]

694
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:49,065
HOT BODY

695
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:50,650
It's because you're so strong.

696
00:26:50,651 --> 00:26:53,236
- That's part of his charm.
- [Suyeon] Exactly.

697
00:26:53,237 --> 00:26:55,780
I didn't tell you because I was
afraid you'd get angry.

698
00:26:55,781 --> 00:26:57,032
And I was a bit embarrassed.

699
00:26:57,533 --> 00:26:59,242
I thought Bokgil would be good-looking,

700
00:26:59,243 --> 00:27:00,786
but he's really not.

701
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:06,415
BOKGIL AND SUYEON REALLY WERE LOVERS

702
00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:09,919
When a man and woman date for a long time…

703
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:11,213
TAKEN ABACK

704
00:27:11,797 --> 00:27:13,172
Sooner or later,

705
00:27:13,173 --> 00:27:15,967
- you cross a line you shouldn't.
- You crossed it.

706
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:18,302
A relationship like ours
is forbidden in these times.

707
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:21,139
- That's why you planned to run away.
- Yes, far away.

708
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:23,766
We planned to run away tonight,

709
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:26,602
but because of this murder case,
here we are.

710
00:27:26,603 --> 00:27:28,020
But

711
00:27:28,021 --> 00:27:29,773
in Musoe's kitchen ceiling,

712
00:27:30,399 --> 00:27:35,236
she kept a book saying pregnant women
should avoid cooling foods like buckwheat

713
00:27:35,237 --> 00:27:38,698
and an excess of stimulating herbs
like cinnamon twigs and ginger.

714
00:27:38,699 --> 00:27:42,451
It's a book called
<i>Compendium of Secret Remedies</i>.

715
00:27:42,452 --> 00:27:45,079
Things like buckwheat
are bad for pregnant women.

716
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:47,957
- She put them in her food intentionally?
- [Hwiryeong] It's possible.

717
00:27:47,958 --> 00:27:50,167
Musoe was in love with Bokgil,

718
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:52,879
but he got Suyeon pregnant,
so out of jealousy,

719
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:55,006
she tried to induce a miscarriage

720
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:57,508
- and fed her buckwheat.
- You rotten brat!

721
00:27:57,509 --> 00:27:59,510
- [Hwiryeong] That's it.
- That's so chilling.

722
00:27:59,511 --> 00:28:02,096
It's true that I was jealous.

723
00:28:02,097 --> 00:28:03,098
I was jealous,

724
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:05,684
so when she didn't get her period,

725
00:28:06,226 --> 00:28:09,854
I did that out of jealousy.

726
00:28:09,855 --> 00:28:12,232
- [Bokgil] It was Musoe's doing.
- [gasps] You tried to kill me?

727
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:15,109
Not you, just your baby.

728
00:28:15,110 --> 00:28:17,905
- That's even worse! It's even more cruel.
- [others laugh]

729
00:28:18,488 --> 00:28:22,408
MUSOE PLANNED REVENGE
BY COOKING WITH BUCKWHEAT

730
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:25,202
[Hwiryeong]
What were you doing last night, Lord Yun?

731
00:28:25,203 --> 00:28:26,370
I got up at the Hour of the Ox.

732
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:28,164
- Around 1 o'clock?
- Yes.

733
00:28:28,165 --> 00:28:29,790
Between the Traveler's room

734
00:28:29,791 --> 00:28:33,127
and my bedroom
is where the victim lay dead.

735
00:28:33,128 --> 00:28:35,379
If I left him there,
I knew I'd be the prime suspect.

736
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:38,132
Did you hear that sound at the end?

737
00:28:38,133 --> 00:28:39,592
- That dragging sound?
- Yes.

738
00:28:39,593 --> 00:28:42,721
I was the one who dragged him
and moved him over there.

739
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:52,188
AFTER FINDING THE BODY,
HE DRAGGED IT TO THE COURTYARD

740
00:28:52,189 --> 00:28:54,398
That's why there's a trail here.

741
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:56,068
But I didn't kill him.

742
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:58,402
Well, that's a bit suspicious.

743
00:28:58,403 --> 00:29:00,363
You could have just woken us up by saying,

744
00:29:00,364 --> 00:29:02,615
- "There's a dead body here!"
- Yeah.

745
00:29:02,616 --> 00:29:05,201
- Instead, you dragged the body…
- [Suyeon] Himself.

746
00:29:05,202 --> 00:29:06,869
[sighs] I find that a bit…

747
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,037
It's because I'm in exile,

748
00:29:08,038 --> 00:29:09,664
and something like this

749
00:29:09,665 --> 00:29:11,624
could lead to greater trouble.

750
00:29:11,625 --> 00:29:14,335
I can't risk arousing suspicion,
so that's why I moved the body.

751
00:29:14,336 --> 00:29:17,338
The victim bled out
in front of my dad's room,

752
00:29:17,339 --> 00:29:19,674
and the way he handled the body…

753
00:29:19,675 --> 00:29:21,384
I find that the most suspicious.

754
00:29:21,385 --> 00:29:26,305
I think my father has
some kind of political secret.

755
00:29:26,306 --> 00:29:29,100
I think him and the Traveler
may have been in on it together.

756
00:29:29,101 --> 00:29:31,894
Like they could be accomplices.

757
00:29:31,895 --> 00:29:34,480
What were thee doing
at the time, Mr. Traveler?

758
00:29:34,481 --> 00:29:35,898
- "Thee"?
- "Thee."

759
00:29:35,899 --> 00:29:36,900
[Suyeon] Old language is hard.

760
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:39,945
[host] <i>Round 3 is over.</i>

761
00:29:40,529 --> 00:29:41,654
What?

762
00:29:41,655 --> 00:29:44,949
[host] <i>A new zone will open in Round 4.</i>

763
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:47,995
<i>Please move to the back.</i>

764
00:29:49,371 --> 00:29:50,706
What's this?

765
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:53,165
[♪ traditional music playing]

766
00:29:53,166 --> 00:29:54,584
[exclaims]

767
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:58,963
THE SHAMAN ZONE

768
00:29:58,964 --> 00:30:00,841
- [Suyeon gasps]
- [Igyeong] It's a shaman.

769
00:30:01,383 --> 00:30:02,842
Hello.

770
00:30:02,843 --> 00:30:04,385
What is this place?

771
00:30:04,386 --> 00:30:05,720
What is this zone for?

772
00:30:05,721 --> 00:30:07,138
Did you bring the number cards?

773
00:30:07,139 --> 00:30:08,765
Number cards? These?

774
00:30:09,433 --> 00:30:11,684
SCROLL CLUE

775
00:30:11,685 --> 00:30:13,811
OPEN A SCROLL THAT MATCHES THE NUMBER

776
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:16,856
OF THE RANDOM BONUS CARD
THAT CAME WITH THE OBJECT CLUE

777
00:30:16,857 --> 00:30:19,693
I'll go first. Unlucky number four.

778
00:30:20,402 --> 00:30:22,528
[♪ ominous music playing]

779
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:23,530
Number four.

780
00:30:25,574 --> 00:30:27,951
- [Bokgil] What's that?
- [Suyeon gasps]

781
00:30:29,494 --> 00:30:31,245
[Bokgil] Read it aloud.

782
00:30:31,246 --> 00:30:32,496
[Suyeon] "Warning."

783
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:35,791
"Lowborn children are dying
due to the terrible famine."

784
00:30:35,792 --> 00:30:39,503
"The evil practice of replacing
noble babies with lowborn babies

785
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:41,505
is all too common."

786
00:30:41,506 --> 00:30:44,300
"Guard your children well

787
00:30:44,301 --> 00:30:46,887
and prepare for the worst."

788
00:30:47,471 --> 00:30:50,097
Someone's switching them.

789
00:30:50,098 --> 00:30:51,850
Kids are being switched?

790
00:30:52,434 --> 00:30:53,727
[Hwiryeong] All right, then.

791
00:30:54,603 --> 00:30:56,187
Here's my number.

792
00:30:56,188 --> 00:30:57,189
Number two.

793
00:30:58,565 --> 00:31:00,816
- Oh, my. What is that?
- [Bokgil] Gosh.

794
00:31:00,817 --> 00:31:01,901
[Suyeon] What does it say?

795
00:31:01,902 --> 00:31:04,987
[Igyeong]
"I've lived someone else's life."

796
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:06,739
- Someone else's life?
- "I had to grow up

797
00:31:06,740 --> 00:31:08,574
as a lowly servant."

798
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:10,409
"He is the cause

799
00:31:10,410 --> 00:31:13,579
of all my suffering."

800
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:16,040
"I shall pay him back with your blood."

801
00:31:16,041 --> 00:31:17,374
That's so scary. What does it mean?

802
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:18,585
It's written in blood.

803
00:31:19,461 --> 00:31:22,296
[Igyeong] <i>They were switched as a child,
so their life was upturned.</i>

804
00:31:22,297 --> 00:31:23,465
A CHANGE IN STATUS?

805
00:31:32,474 --> 00:31:34,016
They were born into a noble family,

806
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:35,602
but they grew up poor.

807
00:31:38,647 --> 00:31:41,525
BIRTH CHAMBER LOG

808
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,529
This is

809
00:31:46,530 --> 00:31:47,531
about me?

810
00:32:15,267 --> 00:32:17,269
Translated by Hannah Og Nam
